 r←IsOldDocsRequest path;p;index
⍝ Tells whether `path` asks for a page of the documentation Tatin used to serve itself.
⍝ Those pages lived in "Assets/docs/", reachable both with and without the REST version
⍝ prefix, until the documentation moved to aplteam.github.io; see `RedirectToDocs`.
⍝ "/v1/documentation" was their index. No folder of that name ever existed: the page was
⍝ generated by `CreateDocumentationIndex`, which went the same way as the pages it listed.
⍝ A "/" is appended before the index is looked for so that it matches on a complete segment
⍝ only. Otherwise "/v1/documentationhelper" would match too, and a package of that name
⍝ would be redirected away instead of served.
 p←(⎕C path),'/'
 index←'/v1/documentation/'
 r←(∨/'/assets/docs/'⍷p)∨index≡(≢index)↑p
⍝Done
